rcial supply agreements or DOE allocations for physical HALEU supply. Its proposed transportation subsidiary represents a conceptual container development effort rather than a fuel enrichment source.3. Capital Structure, Operating Cash Burn, and Dilution HistoryDeveloping advanced nuclear reactors requires substantial capital prior to revenue generation. Evaluating cash reserves, operating burn, capital expenditures, and equity dilution trajectories highlights significant financial divergence across developers.NuScale Power (NYSE: SMR)Cash & Liquid Assets: $1.893 billion total liquidity reported as of June 30, 2026 ($766.5 million in cash and cash equivalents, $305.7 million in short-term investments, and $820.8 million in long-term investments).Quarterly Cash Burn: Q2 2026 operating loss was $64.0 million (compared to an operating loss of $43.1 million in Q2 2025). Six-month cumulative net loss reached $96.75 million.Revenue Profile: Q2 2026 revenue was $75,000 (down 99.1% YoY from $8.054 million in Q2 2025) following the completion of FEED Phase 2 engineering work for RoPower. Trailing Twelve Months (TTM) revenue stands at $10.7 million.24-Month Equity Raises & ATM History: Fully utilized a $1.0 billion At-The-Market (ATM) program in H1 2026, issuing 89,727,165 shares of Class A common stock for $984.5 million in net proceeds at a weighted average price of $11.14. In Q3 2025, sold 13.2 million shares via an earlier ATM program, generating $475.2 million gross.Share Count & Dilution: Class A common shares outstanding expanded from 318.5 million as of December 31, 2025, to 410.4 million as of June 30, 2026 (a 28.8% dilution in Class A shares over six months). Total share count across Class A and Class B stands at ~429.8 million.Going-Concern Disclosures: None present in recent SEC filings.Oklo Inc. (NYSE: OKLO)Cash & Liquid Assets: $3.006 billion in cash, cash equivalents, and marketable securities as of June 30, 2026.Quarterly Cash Burn: Q2 2026 net loss doubled YoY to $48.54 million. Full-year 2026 operating cash burn guidance was raised to $120 million–$150 million, and capital expenditure guidance was increased to $400 million–$500 million, resulting in an aggregate quarterly burn rate of ~$130 million–$162.5 million.Revenue Profile: Q2 2026 revenue was $1.21 million, derived entirely from acquired engineering service subsidiaries rather than nuclear power or isotope sales. TTM revenue is $1.21 million.24-Month Equity Raises & ATM History: Completed its De-SPAC business combination with AltC Acquisition Corp. in May 2024. Launched a $1.0 billion ATM program in May 2026, which was fully exhausted within four months. On September 11, 2026, Oklo launched a second $1.0 billion ATM program authorizing further Class A share sales into the open market.Share Count & Dilution: Class A common shares outstanding reached 185.09 million as of August 7, 2026. Successive $1.0B ATM offerings have caused dilution for pre-merger public shareholders.Going-Concern Disclosures: None present in 2026 SEC filings.X-Energy, Inc. (NASDAQ: XE)Cash & Liquid Assets: $1.90 billion in total liquidity (cash, cash equivalents, and short- and long-term investments) as of June 30, 2026.Quarterly Cash Burn: Q2 2026 net operating cash burn was $97.3 million, with CapEx of $63.3 million (directed toward TX-1 construction), totaling $160.6 million in quarterly cash use. Q2 operating expenses totaled $164.6 million.Revenue Profile: Q2 2026 revenue and grant income totaled $54.6 million ($50.1 million in engineering services and $4.5 million in DOE grant income), up 154% YoY. Q1 2026 revenue was $39.9 million, bringing H1 2026 total revenue to $94.5 million.24-Month Equity Raises & ATM History: Completed an initial public offering on Nasdaq in April 2026, raising $1.02 billion in gross proceeds ($1.1 billion net proceeds) by issuing 44.3 million Class A shares at $23.00 per share.Share Count & Dilution: Non-GAAP fully diluted share count stands at 414 million shares (comprising 280 million Class A shares and 119 million Class B shares) as of August 2026.Going-Concern Disclosures: None following the April 2026 capital raise.Nano Nuclear Energy Inc. (NASDAQ: NNE)Cash & Liquid Assets: $580.0 million in cash, cash equivalents, and short-term Treasury securities as of June 30, 2026 ($298.5M cash + $281.5M short-term investments).Quarterly Cash Burn: Operating cash burn runs at ~$10.0 million–$15.0 million per quarter.Revenue Profile: $0.00 (Pre-revenue).24-Month Equity Raises & ATM History: Listed via Nasdaq IPO in May 2024, raising ~$10.2 million gross. Subsequently executed multiple secondary equity offerings and ATM issuances throughout 2024, 2025, and early 2026, expanding cash reserves from under $10 million to $580 million.Share Count & Dilution: Issued and outstanding common shares grew from ~30.5 million at inception to 53,698,146 shares as of August 10, 2026 (>75% share count expansion in 24 months).Going-Concern Disclosures: Resolved via capital raises.Terrestrial Energy Inc. (NASDAQ: IMSR)Cash & Liquid Assets: Less than $15.0 million in cash and cash equivalents.Quarterly Cash Burn: Free cash flow is negative $15.0 million annually (~$3.75 million–$5.0 million quarterly operating cash burn).Revenue Profile: $0.00 (Pre-revenue).24-Month Equity Raises & ATM History: Listed via De-SPAC business combination with Hennessy Capital Investment Corp. VI ($HOND). Executed capital draws under equity purchase facilities with Yorkville Advisors.Share Count & Dilution: Total common shares outstanding stand at ~105.8 million.Going-Concern Disclosures: Active Disclosure. SEC filings explicitly disclose that the company has less than one year of cash runway based on its free cash flow trend (-$15M FCF), creating continuous liquidity risk.4. Offtake Architecture: Binding Commitments vs. Non-Binding FrameworksEvaluations of commercial backlog require a strict division between binding supply contracts and non-binding frameworks.Binding Contracts: Definitive PPAs, EPC contracts, or purchase orders carrying legally enforceable cancellation penalties or non-refundable cash earnest deposits.Non-Binding Frameworks: MOUs, LOIs, Master Power Agreements (MPAs), and memorandum frameworks carrying zero counterparty financial liability or power purchase obligations.NuScale Power (NYSE: SMR)Binding Capacity: 0.00 GW.Non-Binding Capacity: ~6.46 GW.ENTRA1 / TVA Framework: Strategic agreement with ENTRA1 Energy and Tennessee Valley Authority (TVA) announced in September 2025 targeting up to 6.0 GW of SMR capacity. The counterparty is ENTRA1 (NuScale's development platform); TVA holds no binding legal obligation to execute final PPAs.RoPower (Doicești, Romania): Non-binding framework for a 6-module (462 MWe) SMR plant. FEED Phase 2 engineering was completed, but binding construction contracts remain unexecuted.Prepayments Received: Recognized a $495.0 million Milestone Contribution payment expense payable to ENTRA1 in Q3 2025 under its Master Partnership Agreement.Oklo Inc. (NYSE: OKLO)Binding Capacity: 0.00 GW.Non-Binding Capacity: 12.0+ GW.Switch Master Power Agreement: Executed a non-binding master framework agreement with data center operator Switch targeting 12.0 GW. Switch holds zero legal obligation or financial liability to take power if Oklo fails to secure licensing or construct powerhouses.Prepayments Received: $0.00. Offtake frameworks contain no cash earnest prepayments.X-Energy, Inc. (NASDAQ: XE)Binding Capacity: 0.00 GW Commercial PPAs.Federal Backstop: Supported by a $2.1 billion total potential cost-share allocation under the DOE Advanced Reactor Demonstration Program (ARDP), under which X-Energy has received $547 million in cumulative cash reimbursements as of June 30, 2026.Non-Binding Commercial Pipeline: 11.5 GW.Dow Chemical (Seadrift, TX): Anchor commercial project targeting a 4-unit Xe-100 plant (320 MWe / 800 MWt) for industrial steam and power. Final binding commercial operating contracts remain subject to project milestones.Amazon Framework: Non-binding agreement to evaluate Xe-100 deployments for Amazon Web Services data centers.Prepayments Received: Direct cash reimbursements of $547 million received from the US DOE under ARDP cost-share agreements. Commercial customer prepayments stand at zero.Nano Nuclear Energy Inc. (NASDAQ: NNE)Binding Capacity: 0.00 GW.Non-Binding Capacity: 0.00 GW Commercial.Announcements consist of academic research collaborations (e.g., University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign) and technical study MOUs. No commercial end-user power purchase obligations exist.Prepayments Received: $0.00.Terrestrial Energy Inc. (NASDAQ: IMSR)Binding Capacity: 0.00 GW.Non-Binding Capacity: Early industrial evaluation frameworks (including a site reservation at Texas A&M RELLIS campus).Prepayments Received: $0.00.5. Westinghouse Electric and the eVinci MicroreactorWestinghouse Electric Company represents a major reactor vendor across Generation III+ (AP1000), small modular (AP300), and microreactor (eVinci) platforms. Westinghouse is not directly listed on public exchanges; equity exposure must be accessed through parent entities.WESTINGHOUSE CORPORATE AND CAPITAL STRUCTURE

