Current Ownership StructureWestinghouse is owned by Cameco Corporation (NYSE: CCJ / TSX: CCO), holding a 49% strategic stake, and Brookfield Asset Management (NYSE: BAM) / Brookfield Renewable Partners, holding a controlling 51% stake, following their joint acquisition in late 2023.Proposed IPO & $80 Billion US Government Strategic Partnership$80 Billion Strategic Partnership: In October 2025, Cameco, Brookfield, and the US Department of Commerce executed a binding term sheet for a strategic partnership to finance, permit, and construct new Westinghouse reactors in the US with an aggregate value of at least $80 billion.Participation Interest Structure: The US Government was granted a Participation Interest entitling it to receive 20% of cash distributions in excess of $17.5 billion made by Westinghouse.January 2029 Final Investment Decision (FID) Trigger:For the Participation Interest to vest, the US Government and project partners must execute definitive agreements to reach FID on at least $80 billion in new Westinghouse reactor projects on or prior to January 2029.Warrant Mechanics & IPO Framework:Prior to or upon an IPO, the Participation Interest converts into a 5-year warrant to purchase equity securities equivalent to 20% of the public market valuation after deducting $17.5 billion.If Westinghouse completes an IPO on or prior to January 2029 at a valuation of $30 billion, the government's warrant exercise would result in an effective ~8% equity ownership stake.Stated Timeline: Corporate disclosures target a potential Westinghouse public offering by or before January 2029, dependent on power market conditions and the execution of the $80B project pipeline.The eVinci Microreactor: Technical & Regulatory ProfilePower Output & Core Design: Rated at 5 MWe (15 MWt). Uses HALEU TRISO fuel encapsulated in a solid graphite core block. Core heat is removed passively via 24-foot liquid sodium heat pipes operating on phase-change capillary action, eliminating pumps and primary water loops.Regulatory & Criticality Testing Status:Front-End Engineering: Completed Front-End Engineering and Experiment Design (FEEED) for a prototype test at Idaho National Laboratory's NRIC DOME facility.Criticality Testing: In August 2026, Westinghouse completed zero-power nuclear criticality testing for the eVinci reactor core at the National Criticality Experiments Research Center (NCERC) in Nevada, validating core physics models prior to full-power tests.Commercialization Timeline: Factory setup at the Etna, Pennsylvania manufacturing hub targets high-rate fleet production by 2029–2030, aiming for an initial output of 1 to 2 commercial 5 MWe units per year.Public Investment PathwaysPublic investors cannot purchase direct equity in Westinghouse or eVinci. Public market exposure is accessible via:Cameco Corporation (NYSE: CCJ): Direct access providing 49% net equity earnings exposure to Westinghouse alongside Cameco's core uranium mining and fuel services operations.Brookfield Asset Management (NYSE: BAM): Infrastructure asset manager holding the 51% controlling stake.6. Commercialization Timelines and Schedule SlippageAdvanced reactor commercialization has historically experienced multi-year schedule revisions. Tracking original baseline target dates against current management guidance reveals schedule slippages across all major developers.COMMERCIAL POWER SCHEDULE SLIPPAGE SUMMARY

