ation of Lead UAMPS Project: In late 2023, NuScale and UAMPS mutually terminated the flagship 6-module INL project due to inflation-driven target power price increases (rising from $58/MWh to $89/MWh), leaving NuScale without an active domestic construction site.Q2 2026 Revenue Collapse: Reported Q2 2026 revenue of $75,000 (a 99.1% YoY collapse), missing consensus analyst estimates ($8.8M) due to the expiration of RoPower FEED engineering contracts.Analyst Downgrades: In August–September 2026, investment firms downgraded SMR stock; UBS lowered its rating to "Sell" ($6.00 price target), Citi downgraded to "Sell" ($6.50 target), and RBC cut its target to $10.00, citing extended cash burn and revenue drops.Partner Outflow Obligation: Recognized a $495.0 million milestone contribution payment obligation in Q3 2025 payable to ENTRA1 Energy under global distribution agreements, driving net losses.Oklo Inc. (NYSE: OKLO)Q2 2026 Financial Miss & Burn Guidance Increase: Missed Q2 2026 earnings expectations (adjusted EPS -$0.28 vs. -$0.16 consensus) while net loss doubled YoY to $48.54 million. Concurrently raised full-year 2026 operating cash burn guidance to $120M–$150M and CapEx guidance to $400M–$500M.Internal Control Weaknesses: Disclosed material internal control weaknesses in Form 10-K filings regarding accounting for complex financial instruments and de-SPAC equity transactions.Dilution Impact: Exhausted a $1.0 billion ATM equity program within four months and filed a second $1.0 billion ATM program in September 2026, contributing to a ~45% stock decline from mid-2026 highs due to dilution concerns.X-Energy, Inc. (NASDAQ: XE)Expanding Operating Losses: Q1 2026 net loss widened 252% YoY to $166.2 million ($7.57 loss per share). Q2 2026 operating expenses expanded 156% YoY to $164.6 million.Post-IPO Share Pressure: Shares traded down ~35% from the April 2026 IPO price of $23.00 to $17–$19 per share due to cash burn and heavy capital expenditures for the TX-1 fuel facility.Historical SPAC Collapse: An initial 2022–2023 attempt to list publicly via a SPAC merger was terminated due to adverse market conditions, delaying public capital access until April 2026.Terrestrial Energy Inc. (NASDAQ: IMSR)Active Going-Concern Liquidity Risk: Form 10-Q filings explicitly disclose that the company has less than one year of cash runway based on its negative annual free cash flow (-$15.0 million).Equity Negative Balance Sheet: Disclosed negative total equity (-$6.4 million) and received "Sell" ratings from independent research groups (Weiss Ratings, Wall Street Zen) citing balance sheet risks.Investment Hypotheses and Falsification CriteriaNuScale Power (NYSE: SMR)Core Investment Hypothesis: ENTRA1 Energy successfully converts its non-binding 6 GW TVA framework and Romanian RoPower site studies into definitive EPC contracts with firm equipment down-payments. This would generate module manufacturing revenue and validate NuScale's $1.89B balance sheet without requiring further equity dilution.Falsification Criteria: RoPower defers Final Investment Decision (FID) or TVA fails to execute binding module supply orders by 2027, leaving NuScale with zero active construction sites while quarterly operating cash burn ($60M+) consumes liquid reserves.Oklo Inc. (NYSE: OKLO)Core Investment Hypothesis: Oklo secures formal NRC application acceptance for its Aurora design without major safety review delays, completes construction of its INL demonstration reactor by 2028, and converts its 12 GW Switch framework into legally binding long-term PPAs that support debt financing.Falsification Criteria: The NRC imposes multi-year pre-application review delays, or domestic HALEU enrichment capacity fails to scale by 2028, leaving Oklo unable to fuel its INL reactor while the company continues to issue shares under its sequential $1.0B ATM programs.X-Energy, Inc. (NASDAQ: XE)Core Investment Hypothesis: The NRC issues a Construction Permit for the Dow Seadrift site on its e